WEBVTT

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:13.490
Please enter your resurrection spell.

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:06.310
Enter

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:06.310
KAZUMASREALLYTHEBESTKONOSUBACHARACTER

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.980
The spell is incorrect.
Your quest book has been erased.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:13.490
Enter

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.490
GODSBLESSINGSONTHISWONDERFULWORLD TWO

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.560
<i>My name is Satou Kazuma...</i>

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.560
<i>A foreigner from a distant land,
fated to battle the Devil King.</i>

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.160
<i>Guided by a goddess of fate, 
I was reincarnated in another world...</i>

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:26.440
<i>An unfamiliar world swirling 
with destruction and chaos.</i>

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:28.670
<i>But I have allies that 
I share strong bonds with.</i>

00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.820
<i>The ultimate wizard, a 
noble and beautiful knight,</i>

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.240
<i>and a magnanimous goddess who 
willingly came to my aid.</i>

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:37.640
<i>The gears of fate now begin to turn.</i>

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.140
<i>In order to save this wonderful world,</i>

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.230
<i>our adventure now begins once again!</i>

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.940
You're coming with me!

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.960
Wait, no!

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:09.000
<b>Episode 1  Give Me Deliverance From This Judicial Injustice!</b>

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.210
I wanna go home...

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.170
I just want to go back to Japan.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.180
I'm Sena, the public prosecutor 
assigned by the kingdom.

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.800
Adventurer Satou Kazuma,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:18.720
you are currently suspected of 
the crime of subversion to the state.

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:21.940
Hey, Kazuma, what did you do this time?!

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.430
Come on, apologize!

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.140
I'll tell them I'm sorry, too, 
so hurry up and apologize!

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:28.610
What do you mean, "this time"?!

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:30.440
You should know I didn't do anything!

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:33.880
The coronatite that was 
teleported at your instruction

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:35.820
blew up the residence of a lord.

00:01:37.180 --> 00:01:39.300
Thankfully, there were no fatalities...

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:44.030
But there is the question of whether you are 
a terrorist, or a servant of the Devil King.

00:01:44.920 --> 00:01:46.290
Wait a minute, please.

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.750
If not for Kazuma, there could've been 
worse casualties in the Destroyer battle.

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.280
Megumin...

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:57.260
The only crimes Kazuma commits are 
minor ones, like sexual harassment.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.010
Miss Prosecutor, this must be some mistake.

00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:00.930
Darkness...

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.420
This man lacks the guts for such an act.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:07.060
Despite eyeing me like a 
wild animal in the mansion,

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:10.100
he is the kind of sadsack who 
never once came to my bedside.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:12.410
I-I-I wasn't eyeing anything!

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:15.290
Don't get a big head just because 
your body's somewhat sexy!

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:17.700
I reserve the right to be selective!

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:21.700
Wh-Why, you... And after everything 
you made me do in the bath!

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:24.630
That was because I was under 
that succubus's control!

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.460
You're the one who went along 
with it and washed my back!

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.460
Just how easy are you?!

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.670
Th-Then you do remember, after all!

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.020
Maybe I do!

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:37.810
And as a Crusader who serves Eris-sama, 
my body must remain pure!

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.850
And you call me easy...

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:40.100
Yep!

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.130
I'll kill you dead!

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:42.930
Do it, then!

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:42.930
That's right!

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.640
Kazuma might be an adventurer, 
but he's no criminal!

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.610
This is abuse of state power!

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.270
Adventurers deserve freedom!

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:57.910
Freedom! Freedom! Freedom! Freedom!

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.910
Incidentally, he's not the only one 
the subversion charge may apply to.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:03.280
I won't stop anyone who wants 
to join him in prison, but...

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.790
Screw you guys! Try harder! 
Keep the protest going!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:11.240
If I remember right, Kazuma said 
something like this at the time.

00:03:11.240 --> 00:03:13.810
"It's okay. I'll take responsibility."

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:16.770
"I may not look it, but I 
apparently have good luck!"

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.380
Wait, hang on...

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.080
If...

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:20.610
If?!

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:23.170
If I had been there at the time,

00:03:23.170 --> 00:03:25.710
I'm sure I could've stopped Kazuma!

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.640
But since I wasn't there,
there's nothing I could have done!

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.270
Nope, nothing at all!

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.340
You people...

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:34.230
Wait. Th-That's right.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.690
I was the one who did it!

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:37.040
It was my command!

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:38.860
So please, let me enjoy 
this imprisonment play...

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:40.990
No, let me bear the intensity 
of this punishment!

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.410
Excuse me? I was told you were 
trying to act as a meatshield.

00:03:44.410 --> 00:03:45.450
Meat—

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.370
Wow, haven't seen that in a while.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:51.240
Uh, the Teleport spell was cast by—

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:52.580
Don't, Wiz!

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:52.580
Aqua-sama?!

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.780
If only one of us has to take the 
fall here, that's for the best!

00:03:55.780 --> 00:03:57.480
It might be hard, but suck it up!

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.170
Suck it up for now!

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:03.820
We'll just wait until Kazuma 
finishes doing his time!

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:06.100
Don't make it sound like I 
have to get sent to prison!

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.670
And besides, even if you 
guys don't back me up,

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:10.720
my friends at the Guild are by my side!

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:19.950
Er, um...

00:04:19.950 --> 00:04:21.650
Oh, look at the dust...

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:24.700
You're coming with me!

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:30.250
Damn it... So much for the town where 
new adventurers get their start.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:31.730
If this was a game,

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:35.210
one of those cliché resistance armies 
would come and rescue me...

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:41.690
What the?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:43.340
Kazuma! Kazuma!

00:04:43.940 --> 00:04:45.090
Aqua?

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:47.340
What are you doing here?!

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:49.590
I came to save you, obviously!

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:51.520
I'd never abandon a dear friend.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:54.020
Why not defend me in the first place, then?

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.250
Megumin just used her explosion 
magic on the outskirts of town.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.530
Thanks to that, the guards 
ran off to investigate!

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:07.530
Darkness should be running away with 
the depleted Megumin as we speak.

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:11.290
But won't I be making 
things worse by running?

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:15.020
I hear you can be executed 
for subversive activities.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:16.830
You're just an adventurer 
whose identity is suspect.

00:05:16.830 --> 00:05:19.420
They'll manipulate the truth, 
and you'll end up dead!

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.510
<i>This parallel world really does have the 
cultural level of the Middle Ages...</i>

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.710
But how do I even get out of here?

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.750
First, use that wire to pick the cell's lock.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:39.730
After that, you can use your 
Stealth skill to escape the jail!

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:42.860
Then, once we get back to the mansion, 
we get ready to skip town!

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.770
Well, I'll be waiting out front!

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.580
<i>It's a combination lock...</i>

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.670
Out!

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:57.580
Guess I'll sleep.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:12.930
Kazuma! Hey, Kazuma, wake up!

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.100
You're here again?

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:19.450
What happened yesterday?
Is everybody okay?

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.800
The other two made it back 
without being spotted,

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:26.180
but they were accused of being 
behind the explosion.

00:06:25.710 --> 00:06:26.740
Were they, now?

00:06:26.180 --> 00:06:28.990
We shouldn't underestimate this 
world's investigative ability.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.710
I dunno about that...

00:06:29.430 --> 00:06:30.860
But it's okay.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:31.110
What is?

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:35.330
I forced them to wear masks today, 
so they won't be found out!

00:06:35.630 --> 00:06:38.080
<i>The problem is the explosion magic.</i>

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:42.700
More importantly, I waited all night 
for you. Why didn't you escape?

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.120
Snow accumulated on my head,

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:46.870
and they kept dragging me in for questioning!

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:48.530
The lock uses a combination.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:50.520
That's clever of them.

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:54.480
I never imagined they'd have such foolproof 
measures in place to prevent escape.

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.640
But today I've got the perfect solution!

00:06:57.470 --> 00:06:58.810
<i>A hacksaw?</i>

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.770
You're gonna cut the bars with that?

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.590
Very astute of you!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.770
We don't have much time, 
so let's work together.

00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.280
Hurry it up!

00:07:10.510 --> 00:07:12.240
Except I can't reach up there.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:15.500
Not a problem. I'm not stupid, you know.

00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:17.700
I brought something for you to stand on, too!

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.460
<i>Eureka.</i>

00:07:20.140 --> 00:07:22.000
And how will you get it in here?

00:07:24.140 --> 00:07:25.440
Hang on a second.

00:07:32.190 --> 00:07:33.420
You've got it all wrong!

00:07:33.420 --> 00:07:36.290
Kazuma needs this, so I was 
just giving him a present...

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:39.020
Never heard of a stepping 
box for a present before.

00:07:39.310 --> 00:07:41.150
And what are you doing here at this hour?

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:43.360
Weren't you wandering around yesterday, too?

00:07:42.090 --> 00:07:45.970
Maybe I should learn from how 
optimistic that idiot is.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:48.700
Out!

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:50.780
Guess I'll sleep.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.710
Do you know what this is?

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.170
It's a magical item that 
lets us see through lies.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:08.370
First off, where are you from,

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.880
and what did you do before 
you became an adventurer?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:14.340
<i>They started off with a 
hard-to-answer question.</i>

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.310
I'm from Japan. I was a student there.

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:21.140
Why'd it go off?!

00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:25.400
Where are you from, and what did you do there?

00:08:28.480 --> 00:08:29.750
Hang on!

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:31.710
I wasn't really lying!

00:08:34.900 --> 00:08:37.000
I am from Japan.

00:08:37.330 --> 00:08:41.450
But I stayed home all day, every day, 
living a life of self-indulgence.

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.830
Why pretend to be a student?

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:49.610
I wasn't really pretending...

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:52.130
Oh, never mind.

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.760
<i>Damn it, I hate this thing!</i>

00:08:55.450 --> 00:08:58.530
I've never heard of a 
place called Japan before.

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.850
So, what's your motive for 
becoming an adventurer?

00:09:02.270 --> 00:09:05.780
To save the people who were being 
oppressed by the Devil King—

00:09:10.110 --> 00:09:12.960
I thought being an adventurer seemed cool,

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:14.640
a fun way to make a lot of money,

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:17.360
and a great way to make 
pretty girls fall all over me.

00:09:20.790 --> 00:09:23.320
O-Okay. Well, next question.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.460
Did you have a grudge against the lord?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.250
I've heard that once you got into debt, 
you complained about him regularly.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.450
The reward I received for the dullahan hunt

00:09:32.450 --> 00:09:36.120
took care of the debts I 
owed for the town's repairs.

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.800
Even if we were trying to protect it,

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.470
destroying the town in the process makes 
it a moot point. I understand that.

00:09:44.410 --> 00:09:49.580
That was actually the argument 
I used to convince my friends.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:50.990
I personally felt something like,

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:53.470
"This is how you treat the 
hero who saved this town?!

00:09:53.470 --> 00:09:55.530
You all should die!"

00:09:56.730 --> 00:09:59.840
I-I see. Moving on...

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:01.830
Uh, can I ask you something?

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.860
Can we just get to the point?

00:10:04.860 --> 00:10:09.020
I know I'm repeating myself, 
but I made that call to save the town.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.760
It seems I was wrong.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.590
I had only heard bad rumors about you, so...

00:10:19.920 --> 00:10:21.720
I apologize.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:23.480
<i>Oh, how nice.</i>

00:10:23.480 --> 00:10:26.360
<i>I guess the harsh treatment 
was just for criminals...</i>

00:10:27.590 --> 00:10:31.240
Honestly, taking rumors 
at face value like that!

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.510
Makes you a bad prosecutor, doesn't it?

00:10:33.510 --> 00:10:34.940
I-I'm sorry...

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.150
Do you know what I've accomplished?

00:10:37.940 --> 00:10:40.710
I contributed the most to our 
subjugation of that dullahan!

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:43.990
We beat the Destroyer thanks to the 
amazing job I did as commander!

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:47.920
And instead of getting any thanks, 
I get accusations instead!

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:50.260
S-Sorry about that!

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:51.910
It's just that this is my job...

00:10:51.910 --> 00:10:54.600
And I do know of your 
accomplishments, Satou-san.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:55.340
But...

00:10:55.340 --> 00:10:56.490
But?

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:58.280
But what, exactly?!

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.450
Also, even after I'm cleared of suspicion,

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:02.530
you guys still don't offer me any tea?

00:11:02.530 --> 00:11:04.880
I'd even take a pork cutlet bowl!

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:06.140
P-Pork cutlet...?

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:08.220
I'm sorry, we don't have 
anything like that...

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:10.230
I can get you some tea right away, though!

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:15.130
It's lukewarm!

00:11:15.130 --> 00:11:17.580
Don't the prosecutors here 
even know how to serve tea?!

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.360
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:21.730
I bet this gap between 
that harsh attitude and

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:24.290
how you are now means you don't 
have a boyfriend, either.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:27.950
I may as well ask! Do you even have a man?

00:11:28.330 --> 00:11:29.160
I do not.

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:34.420
Yes, I realize that my personality is 
why I don't have any male companionship,

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:36.090
in spite of my age.

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:38.050
Are you satisfied?

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:41.510
Please don't get too full of yourself.

00:11:42.790 --> 00:11:44.220
I'm sorry...

00:11:44.220 --> 00:11:47.310
Do you know what you're called around town?

00:11:47.310 --> 00:11:47.840
Huh?

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.450
"Crapuma" and "Kazutrash" and such.

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:54.270
Th-That's horrible! 
What jerks are calling me that?!

00:11:56.090 --> 00:11:58.250
Just for the record, I should ask...

00:11:58.250 --> 00:12:01.600
Do you truly have no connection 
to the Devil King's army?

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.160
No discourse with any of the 
Devil King's leaders or anything?

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:06.900
I have no such thing!

00:12:06.900 --> 00:12:07.660
Do I—

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:14.790
Do I really look... like... that big a deal?

00:12:16.470 --> 00:12:20.230
<i>Crap! Wiz used to be a leader 
in the Devil King's army!</i>

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:37.020
We will now begin the trial 
of the accused, Satou Kazuma.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:54.450
You look really nervous.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:58.880
It's okay. I'll counter that prosecutor's 
arguments until she's in tears.

00:12:59.160 --> 00:13:00.730
Worry not, Kazuma.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.010
You haven't done anything wrong in this case.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.770
<i>That's reassuring.</i>

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:08.720
<i>So reassuring... and yet...</i>

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:12.430
Hey, you can probably just leave it to me!

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.220
<i>This one's the problem.</i>

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:20.750
Hey, hey, that guy seems to 
have his eyes glued to us.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:23.690
That is the lord in question, Aldarp.

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.580
Prosecutor, step forward!

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:37.890
A crime that threatens someone 
with the station of lord

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.040
is a threat to the nation itself.

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:45.260
As such, the accused, Satou Kazuma, is 
charged with subversion of the state's power.

00:13:45.550 --> 00:13:47.760
<b>Witness Questioning</b>

00:13:46.260 --> 00:13:47.760
Bring forth the witness!

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:51.710
Chris!

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:54.770
I guess they called me down for this.

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.230
<b>First Testimony</b>

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:57.230
<b>Satou Kazuma's Underpants Hijacking</b>

00:13:57.700 --> 00:14:01.730
So, Chris-san, he used Steal 
on you in a public place

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:04.680
and removed your underwear, correct?

00:14:05.050 --> 00:14:08.310
Uh... Well, that's correct, but that was...

00:14:08.310 --> 00:14:09.810
I saw it happen!

00:14:12.150 --> 00:14:15.250
I saw him swinging around that 
girl's panties the street!

00:14:15.650 --> 00:14:17.000
Which man do you mean?

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.840
I am satisfied with establishing 
the truth of this evidence.

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:28.040
Thank you very much.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:31.220
<b>Second Testimony</b>

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:31.220
<b>Satou Kazuma's Theft, Illegal Sale of a Magic Sword</b>

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:33.100
Mitsurugi Kyouya-san,

00:14:33.100 --> 00:14:36.290
your magic sword was stolen and 
sold off by the accused, correct?

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.490
W-Well, that's true.

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.810
But I was the one who 
issued the challenge, so—

00:14:41.390 --> 00:14:42.350
Thank you!

00:14:42.350 --> 00:14:43.190
Wait a sec—

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.940
<b>Third Testimony</b>

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:45.940
<b>Satou Kazuma's Threats Against Women</b>

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:49.950
And you two, when you tried 
to retrieve the magic sword,

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.950
he threatened to remove your 
underwear in public, did he not?

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:54.880
That's right, he threatened us!

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.400
He said he was an advocate 
of true gender equality,

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.090
so he had no problem with 
dropkicking a female opponent!

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:00.570
You coward!

00:15:00.570 --> 00:15:01.820
It's true!

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:05.000
"I'll unleash my Steal ability 
right here in public," he said!

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:08.840
I saw it! He was doing this 
creepy thing with his hands...

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.210
It was really quite creepy!

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.600
Thank you very much.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:14.890
What a deviant.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:15.700
That's horrible.

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:16.850
What trash.

00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:18.850
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:21.810
<i>This is getting seriously bad now!</i>

00:15:22.030 --> 00:15:25.070
That's enough. Let's get 
this execution on the road.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.180
Objection!

00:15:26.870 --> 00:15:29.320
I will admit that Kazuma 
has a warped personality,

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:32.700
but all this testimony is 
inadmissible as evidence!

00:15:33.050 --> 00:15:33.910
Megumin!

00:15:34.520 --> 00:15:38.370
I demand some legitimate basis for 
these accusations of terrorism!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.910
Yeah! What're you basing it on?!

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.370
The basis for the case? Very well.

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:43.630
First!

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:48.630
Even if it was to defeat a dullahan, 
he damaged the town with a flood.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:51.130
Second!

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:53.870
The use of explosion magic 
in the vicinity of the town

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:57.730
has altered the landscape and 
ecosystem, on top of creating

00:15:57.730 --> 00:15:59.600
disruptive noise late at night!

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.850
<i>My defense is doomed.</i>

00:16:03.010 --> 00:16:04.310
And third!

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:10.190
An eyewitness report of the accused using a 
skill known only by undead, Drain Touch!

00:16:11.540 --> 00:16:13.950
<i>Stay quiet! Exercise your 
right to remain silent!</i>

00:16:14.280 --> 00:16:16.910
Covering your ears doesn't 
mean that it didn't happen!

00:16:17.570 --> 00:16:19.320
The biggest reason to suspect you

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.790
is the fact that you claimed to have 
no connection the Devil King's army.

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:25.540
At that time, the magic 
lie detector went off!

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:29.420
Is that not sufficient evidence?

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:35.300
It's over, it's all over! 
Kazuma's a convict now!

00:16:35.460 --> 00:16:38.060
Oh, God! What do I do?!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:40.730
Even though he was just 
a shut-in NEET at first!

00:16:38.340 --> 00:16:39.950
That's enough!

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:43.270
There no denying he's connected 
to the Devil King's army!

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:43.270
But first he becomes more 
and more of a pervert,

00:16:43.270 --> 00:16:45.940
and now he's a criminal!

00:16:44.850 --> 00:16:45.940
<i>Thanks, old man.</i>

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:47.860
<i>This is my chance!</i>

00:16:47.950 --> 00:16:51.360
He sent explosives into my mansion!

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.610
Execute him immediately!

00:16:52.610 --> 00:16:53.690
Wrong!

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:56.560
I have no connections to the Devil King's army,

00:16:56.560 --> 00:16:57.990
and I'm no terrorist!

00:16:58.150 --> 00:16:59.730
What point does this serve now?

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:03.120
Your testimony was proven 
wrong, on the record!

00:17:03.120 --> 00:17:05.870
All right, listen up!

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:06.880
I'm gonna say it!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:07.630
I...

00:17:08.090 --> 00:17:12.550
do not work for the Devil King's 
army, nor am I a terrorist!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.160
That can't be!

00:17:19.160 --> 00:17:20.310
Your honor?

00:17:21.050 --> 00:17:22.250
Given the circumstances,

00:17:22.250 --> 00:17:26.270
the prosecution's basis for this case 
can no longer be seen as valid.

00:17:32.140 --> 00:17:34.450
Therefore, the accused, Satou Kazuma,

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:38.140
with no sufficient basis to suspect 
you, I judge you innocent—

00:17:38.140 --> 00:17:40.330
No, Judge.

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.080
Lord Aldarp?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.960
Are you trying to embarrass me?

00:17:48.120 --> 00:17:49.880
What the hell?! That's playing dirty!

00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.460
You're nothing but an adventurer!

00:17:53.070 --> 00:17:55.420
<i>Stupid Middle Ages...</i>

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.220
The defendant... is guilty.

00:17:58.220 --> 00:17:59.930
His sentence...

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:01.850
is death.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:05.600
That's not right!

00:18:06.490 --> 00:18:10.400
Your honor, will you hear me out?

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:13.330
Darkness?

00:18:16.480 --> 00:18:17.240
That's...

00:18:17.660 --> 00:18:19.680
The Dustiness family crest!

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:23.780
The Dustiness family?

00:18:23.780 --> 00:18:27.330
They're said to be the king's 
greatest allies! They're famous!

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:31.840
I knew something was up with that gal...

00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.590
But I never imagined this.

00:18:33.740 --> 00:18:36.190
And after I kept quiet about it for you...

00:18:36.190 --> 00:18:37.620
He's a sly one.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:40.710
Nothing short of this would've 
prevented your execution.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:45.600
Would you let me handle this trial?

00:18:47.390 --> 00:18:50.060
I am not asking for it to be canceled.

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:54.820
With time, I can prove this man's innocence.

00:18:55.290 --> 00:18:57.820
I don't care how much authority 
the Dustiness family wields...

00:18:58.260 --> 00:19:00.710
I would owe you for this.

00:19:01.060 --> 00:19:04.910
That being the case, 
I will do anything you ask.

00:19:08.170 --> 00:19:09.440
Anything?

00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:11.330
Yes, anything.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.690
Darkness-san...

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:13.780
Darkness...

00:19:14.210 --> 00:19:16.890
Th-That's right! 
Kazuma didn't do anything wrong!

00:19:16.890 --> 00:19:18.470
He even gave me a coupon!

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:20.600
This trial's a load of crap!

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:22.430
Kazuma! Kazuma!

00:19:22.430 --> 00:19:27.680
Kazuma! Kazuma! Kazuma! Kazuma!

00:19:27.940 --> 00:19:30.020
Order! Order!

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:35.040
Order, please!

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:37.280
I'm telling you people to pipe down, damn it!

00:19:39.650 --> 00:19:41.280
KO! NO! SU! BA!

00:19:41.770 --> 00:19:42.780
Ahem...

00:19:43.020 --> 00:19:46.320
A request from none other than a 
daughter of the Dustiness family.

00:19:46.320 --> 00:19:48.080
I will believe your words.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:53.790
The accused, Satou Kazuma, 
will be given a stay of trial!

00:19:55.540 --> 00:19:57.140
This is great, Kazuma!

00:19:57.140 --> 00:20:00.380
I don't really get why, but you're not 
getting executed, and that's a good thing!

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:03.030
Hup! A celebratory Nature's Beauty!

00:20:04.130 --> 00:20:06.960
It seems my wit and arguments bore fruit.

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:10.140
You guys gave up with hardly any resistance.

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:13.850
<b>Satou Kazuma is given a stay of trial.
Remains under surveillance as a suspect.</b>

00:20:18.130 --> 00:20:19.990
For once, I really have to be grateful.

00:20:21.710 --> 00:20:23.200
You can't rest easy yet.

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:25.370
But leave Aldarp to me.

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:26.890
Will you be okay?

00:20:26.890 --> 00:20:29.630
That old dude was giving you a nasty look.

00:20:29.630 --> 00:20:31.580
Are you sure he won't 
demand something crazy?

00:20:32.730 --> 00:20:34.540
S-Something crazy...

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:37.790
I want a refund for my concern.

00:20:37.790 --> 00:20:39.250
No, it'll be fine.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:43.260
I'll be taking my leave now.

00:20:48.280 --> 00:20:49.280
Lalatina.

00:20:49.280 --> 00:20:51.040
Do not call me that!

00:20:58.410 --> 00:21:00.690
<i>I have two missions now.</i>

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:04.470
<i>First, to prove that I'm not a 
member of the Devil King's forces.</i>

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.950
<i>The second is to reimburse 
the lord for his damages.</i>

00:21:08.520 --> 00:21:12.910
<i>It might not be fair, but after what 
Darkness did to save me, it must be done.</i>

00:21:14.600 --> 00:21:16.450
<i>As of now, my adventure</i>

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:18.700
<i>enters its second chapter!</i>

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.810
The court has ordered

00:21:23.810 --> 00:21:28.250
that the suspect's personal assets 
be seized to pay back his debt!

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:54.020
<i>My adventure's...</i>

00:21:54.370 --> 00:21:56.670
<i>second chapter... starts now...</i>

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.460
<b>Suspect Kazuma's</b>

00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.460
<b>Total Debt</b>

00:21:57.710 --> 00:21:59.460
<b>1,240,000 Eris</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.180
<b>Mom, Dad, it's been a while. I'm currently in a really tough position.
I'm facing a lot of questions about  my choices as an adventurer,
and as a human being. But when I think about the people who are close to me,
I think I can endure anything. I think I'm a guy who can get things done,
when it comes down to it. I used to always say that one day I would
do something big. ...No, I don't mean anything criminal!</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.210
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:40.210
<b>A Friend for This Crimson Demon Girl!</b>

00:23:31.060 --> 00:23:34.510
Mom, Dad, it's been a while.

00:23:34.650 --> 00:23:37.510
I'm currently in a really tough position.

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:40.460
